        "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(10x)}{2{x}^{3}}-1)=$",
        "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since $2{x}^{3}\u226b\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(10x)$ for large values of $x,$ the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(10x)}{2{x}^{3}}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(10x)}{2{x}^{3}}-1)=0-1=-1.\n$$",
